{"v":1,"id":"01KZB7KJFVHJCWYZ9V7BH5Y586","ts":"2026-08-06T09:48:53.627Z","initiative":"writeback-collisions","session":"b872dc9d-fbc5-410f-a3fc-b4a9ac30a614","source":"claude-code","actor":"agent","user":"dev@jithin.io","type":"decision_logged","payload":{"because":"The append is a single O_APPEND write — there is no in-flight window to wait on, and a lease held by a killed agent would deadlock against the Stop hook that blocks exit on a missing write-back. The real defect is that a collision only reaches the NEXT SessionStart, where a fresh agent with no context inherits two next-actions and must guess how they relate; telling the writer at write time reaches an agent that still holds the context to reconcile. Caller-as-reference rather than max(ended) because same-millisecond ties make the winner ambiguous (state.sessions order decides it), and \"differs from what I just wrote\" is the question the caller actually has.","chose":"Return colliding parallel write-backs from sofar_end_session itself — field omitted when none — computed against the CALLER's session as the reference interval, not the fold's max(ended) winner.","over":"Locking/leasing the record so a second writer waits; a daemon-pushed SSE notification; or leaving overlappingWritebacks read-side only."}}
